k2 is imaginary, so imaginary
times imaginary, real.

00:36:15.290 --> 00:36:19.040
It's a negative real, so it's
a negative exponential decay

00:36:19.040 --> 00:36:21.050
function.

00:36:21.050 --> 00:36:29.980
So in this case, what I have
is this is a a ball coming in,

00:36:29.980 --> 00:36:32.860
the particle comes
in, and there is

00:36:32.860 --> 00:36:38.460
a fan at the wave on the
other side of the interface.

00:36:38.460 --> 00:36:40.470
The time-- the average
speaking, there's

00:36:40.470 --> 00:36:42.870
no particle going in
to the other side,

00:36:42.870 --> 00:36:47.460
but the wave function is
now zero on the other side.

00:36:47.460 --> 00:36:50.730
And this wave is called
everlasting wave.

00:36:53.580 --> 00:36:54.470
Evanescent.

00:37:01.220 --> 00:37:09.495
And now what's the
magnitude of those?

00:37:14.300 --> 00:37:21.180
So if you look at your decay
of this evanescent wave,

00:37:21.180 --> 00:37:23.520
if you look at the decay
of evanescent wave,

00:37:23.520 --> 00:37:29.090
it's really the magnitude of
E minus u 2m h-bar squared.

00:37:29.090 --> 00:37:30.060
That's the square root.

00:37:30.060 --> 00:37:31.770
This is really the magnitude.

00:37:31.770 --> 00:37:36.560
So what I have here,
the magnitude of k

00:37:36.560 --> 00:37:46.370
is 2m real E minus
u and h-bar squared.

00:37:46.370 --> 00:37:49.100
That's the k2.

00:37:49.100 --> 00:37:51.770
That's the decay.

00:37:51.770 --> 00:37:54.700
Or u minus E.

00:37:54.700 --> 00:37:59.740
So if I look at the
electron u minus E.

00:37:59.740 --> 00:38:04.030
Let's say we take one
electron volt. So the energy--

00:38:04.030 --> 00:38:12.130
so the order of magnitude is 2
times 9.1 10 to the minus 31.

00:38:12.130 --> 00:38:22.840
And electron volts, one electron
volt is 1.6 10 to the minus 19.

00:38:22.840 --> 00:38:31.480
And h-bar squared, h-bar is
1 10 to the minus 34, so 68.

00:38:31.480 --> 00:38:33.200
So this one is 31.

00:38:33.200 --> 00:38:34.330
19 gives me 50.

00:38:37.360 --> 00:38:44.110
And this gives me
68, so that's 18.

00:38:44.110 --> 00:38:52.820
18 square root is of the order
of 9, and the rest is OK here.

00:38:52.820 --> 00:38:55.420
Maybe I have five.

00:38:55.420 --> 00:38:59.870
Order of line inverse meter.

00:38:59.870 --> 00:39:01.120
OK.

00:39:01.120 --> 00:39:05.320
So that's the magnitude
of this wave extent

00:39:05.320 --> 00:39:08.500
if it's an electron
into the other side.

00:39:08.500 --> 00:39:13.920
It's of the order inverse
of that gives me what?

00:39:13.920 --> 00:39:17.760
2 angstroms, right?

00:39:17.760 --> 00:39:21.480
So it's an evanescent
and rapidly decaying--

00:39:21.480 --> 00:39:24.520
exponentially rapidly decaying
wave on the other side.

00:39:24.520 --> 00:39:29.210
So who cares 2 angstroms, right?

00:39:29.210 --> 00:39:31.940
Then let me tell a story.

00:39:31.940 --> 00:39:34.570
So there was this guy.

00:39:34.570 --> 00:39:39.100
He just finished his PhD
and went to a job interview

00:39:39.100 --> 00:39:41.850
at IBM Zurich.

00:39:41.850 --> 00:39:46.360
And his name is Binnig.

00:39:46.360 --> 00:39:51.280
And the interviewer
asked him, said

00:39:51.280 --> 00:39:56.920
they want to measure
the surface roughness

00:39:56.920 --> 00:39:59.950
to very high precision, asking
him whether he had the ideas

00:39:59.950 --> 00:40:01.820
or not.

00:40:01.820 --> 00:40:04.720
And he thought about
this, and came up

00:40:04.720 --> 00:40:10.280
with the idea that's
using a metal tip,

00:40:10.280 --> 00:40:12.080
and this is a metal surface.

00:40:14.960 --> 00:40:18.980
And he put a bias,
so vacuum here.

00:40:18.980 --> 00:40:20.030
There's an energy level.

00:40:20.030 --> 00:40:24.170
You read the Einstein
work function.

00:40:24.170 --> 00:40:27.800
Maybe you didn't read the--
you read the wave nature,

00:40:27.800 --> 00:40:29.480
the particle nature of light.

00:40:29.480 --> 00:40:32.630
But say there is a few
electron volts gap here,

00:40:32.630 --> 00:40:34.760
the barrier vacuum.

00:40:34.760 --> 00:40:36.560
Work function of metal.

00:40:36.560 --> 00:40:39.750
So here is a few electron volts.

00:40:39.750 --> 00:40:45.800
And he say, if you
bias it with a voltage,

00:40:45.800 --> 00:40:48.480
the electron exponential decay.

00:40:48.480 --> 00:40:51.230
But once they meet the outer
metal, become alive again.

00:40:51.230 --> 00:40:52.310
We'll talk about that.

00:40:52.310 --> 00:40:56.010
That's autonomy of
this evanescent wave.

00:40:56.010 --> 00:41:01.560
And it's very sensitive
to atomic scale bumpiness,

00:41:01.560 --> 00:41:05.020
because this is
angstrom-level exponential.

00:41:05.020 --> 00:41:09.250
So with that, you can measure--

00:41:09.250 --> 00:41:11.590
that's the principle of
scanning tunneling microscope.

00:41:11.590 --> 00:41:14.530
You really can measure
the electron wave function

00:41:14.530 --> 00:41:16.490
on the surface.

00:41:16.490 --> 00:41:19.320
So you can actually
image the atoms.

00:41:19.320 --> 00:41:22.200
And so he got a
Nobel Prize for that.

00:41:22.200 --> 00:41:22.897
OK.

00:41:22.897 --> 00:41:24.480
Hopefully you'll get
a chance when you

00:41:24.480 --> 00:41:28.020
have an interview like that.

00:41:28.020 --> 00:41:30.570
You have to think, you
have to be able to come up

00:41:30.570 --> 00:41:31.830
with the idea, right?

00:41:31.830 --> 00:41:36.720
So that's the quantum work.

00:41:36.720 --> 00:41:38.880
It's going up a hill.

00:41:38.880 --> 00:41:41.350
Now you reverse it.

00:41:41.350 --> 00:41:48.160
You say, "what if my electron
is going backwards from here

00:41:48.160 --> 00:41:50.230
to here?"

00:41:50.230 --> 00:41:51.673
Is there a reflection.

00:41:55.750 --> 00:42:01.770
You look at the derivation,
there's no difference.

00:42:01.770 --> 00:42:05.400
Even if you go downhill,
even if you not go barrier,

00:42:05.400 --> 00:42:09.690
you go a step down, you
still have a reflection.

00:42:09.690 --> 00:42:11.940
You have discontinuity.

00:42:11.940 --> 00:42:13.670
In potential, you
have reflection there.

00:42:18.390 --> 00:42:24.510
So this is, in fact, this
is a Lomer incidence.

00:42:27.340 --> 00:42:31.150
And when you consider
actually electrical interface

00:42:31.150 --> 00:42:34.630
resistance, for example,
electrons can actually

00:42:34.630 --> 00:42:35.560
come to an interface.

00:42:35.560 --> 00:42:38.890
Not just Lomer, it can
come all directions.

00:42:41.850 --> 00:42:44.600
And you should be able
to sit there and do

00:42:44.600 --> 00:42:48.580
any angle in incidents.

00:42:48.580 --> 00:42:52.060
in fact, I check a lot of
electrical engineering book.

00:42:52.060 --> 00:42:53.710
Nobody even did that.

00:42:53.710 --> 00:42:55.415
I was surprised.

00:42:55.415 --> 00:42:57.790
OK, if you're an electrical
engineer, you should do this.

00:43:01.230 --> 00:43:03.780
So this is for electron wave.

00:43:03.780 --> 00:43:08.880
And now let's go, we
say this is scalar wave.

00:43:08.880 --> 00:43:10.260
It's the easiest.

00:43:10.260 --> 00:43:14.370
And let's go to
more complicated.

00:43:14.370 --> 00:43:16.860
And let's look at
the vector wave.

00:43:24.310 --> 00:43:30.170
And vector wave, the least
complicated vector wave

00:43:30.170 --> 00:43:33.560
is the electromagnetic wave.

00:43:33.560 --> 00:43:36.230
EM waves.

00:43:36.230 --> 00:43:40.140
That's probably the big leap
from a Schrodinger equation,

00:43:40.140 --> 00:43:42.440
which is a scalar
equation, which

00:43:42.440 --> 00:43:44.880
is by no means easy to solve.

00:43:44.880 --> 00:43:47.410
We got a model of our electrons.

00:43:47.410 --> 00:43:49.790
They're actually not a good
tool to solve that right now.

00:43:49.790 --> 00:43:52.070
Even if you have two
or three electrons,

00:43:52.070 --> 00:43:55.570
their mutual interaction
becomes very difficult to solve.

00:43:55.570 --> 00:43:57.160
And that's many-body problem.

00:43:57.160 --> 00:44:00.820
But say, let's go to EM waves.

00:44:00.820 --> 00:44:05.510
And for that, you have to
go to Maxwell equations.

00:44:05.510 --> 00:44:09.900
And either you forgot it
or you heard about it.

00:44:09.900 --> 00:44:13.100
So let's rewrite the
Maxwell equations.

00:44:21.150 --> 00:44:25.740
And we have four equations.

00:44:25.740 --> 00:44:29.670
E cross H minus time derivative.

00:44:33.690 --> 00:44:42.450
They cross E, and cross H
is D. Dt plus the current.

00:44:42.450 --> 00:44:54.650
And we have then the divergence
of the displacement field

00:44:54.650 --> 00:44:58.100
equals the charge density.

00:44:58.100 --> 00:45:02.930
And the diverging magnetic
induction is zero.

00:45:02.930 --> 00:45:08.810
And just to review,
this is essentially

00:45:08.810 --> 00:45:10.580
what the first equations say.

00:45:10.580 --> 00:45:13.450
If you change your
magnetic field,

00:45:13.450 --> 00:45:16.140
you have a general
electric field.

00:45:16.140 --> 00:45:22.190
Then secondly, if you pass
a current through a coil,

00:45:22.190 --> 00:45:25.710
you generate a magnetic field.

00:45:25.710 --> 00:45:29.315
And this is the Faraday
law, this is more like

00:45:29.315 --> 00:45:32.060
an Ampére's law.

00:45:32.060 --> 00:45:35.320
Some of the high
school experiment.

00:45:35.320 --> 00:45:41.530
And Maxwell only
add the one term,

00:45:41.530 --> 00:45:44.470
and he got all the credit.

00:45:44.470 --> 00:45:45.430
OK.

00:45:45.430 --> 00:45:53.260
So what we have here, E
is the electric field.

00:45:53.260 --> 00:45:57.430
The electric field
is the gradient

00:45:57.430 --> 00:46:01.270
of electrostatic potential.

00:46:01.270 --> 00:46:04.830
And so the unit is
volt over meter.

00:46:09.490 --> 00:46:16.640
And H is a magnetic
field, and sometimes I

00:46:16.640 --> 00:46:19.850
don't remember the unit, so
I go back to think of this.

00:46:19.850 --> 00:46:22.910
Current density I know.

00:46:22.910 --> 00:46:29.100
Current density here
is m per meter squared.

00:46:29.100 --> 00:46:31.640
So here is the u--
so times 1 meter,

00:46:31.640 --> 00:46:36.340
that gives me magnetic
field as m per meter.

00:46:36.340 --> 00:46:40.780
So magnetic field
is m per meter.

00:46:44.830 --> 00:46:49.060
And D is the electrical
displacement.

00:46:54.110 --> 00:46:55.010
Displacement.

00:47:01.250 --> 00:47:08.210
And what it means is that
if you have a material,

00:47:08.210 --> 00:47:09.320
you have atoms.

00:47:09.320 --> 00:47:13.520
Atoms has electrons,
ions, right?

00:47:13.520 --> 00:47:16.220
If you have an electric
field comes in,

00:47:16.220 --> 00:47:21.730
you know that they
will get polarized.

00:47:21.730 --> 00:47:25.060
Positive charge has a force
along the field direction.

00:47:25.060 --> 00:47:28.850
Negative charge,
opposite field direction.

00:47:28.850 --> 00:47:32.500
So that means they
will have a dipole.

00:47:32.500 --> 00:47:35.830
So you have, in this case,
you have more like a dipole.

00:47:35.830 --> 00:47:39.220
Here is a positive,
here is a negative.

00:47:39.220 --> 00:47:41.350
OK.

00:47:41.350 --> 00:47:48.970
So D is the polarization
per unit volume,

00:47:48.970 --> 00:47:58.580
dipole moment per unit volume,
and plus the-- if you have

00:47:58.580 --> 00:48:03.190
original field comes in,
converting into the same unit--

00:48:03.190 --> 00:48:04.630
so that's a epsilon zero.

00:48:04.630 --> 00:48:05.920
That's a vacuum.

00:48:05.920 --> 00:48:11.020
Plus the polarization per
unit, the dipole moment

00:48:11.020 --> 00:48:12.230
per unit volume.

00:48:12.230 --> 00:48:19.720
So dipole moment is
the charge transmitter,

00:48:19.720 --> 00:48:24.220
and per unit volume is
cubic, so the unit here

00:48:24.220 --> 00:48:25.690
is a coulomb per meter squared.

00:48:29.180 --> 00:48:31.730
And from coulomb
per meter square,

00:48:31.730 --> 00:48:33.620
this is a coulomb
per meter square,

00:48:33.620 --> 00:48:35.810
you find the epsilon zero.

00:48:35.810 --> 00:48:40.310
That's the vacuum permittivity.

00:48:40.310 --> 00:48:44.330
I always say "permeability,"
"permittivity."

00:48:44.330 --> 00:48:50.750
Permittivity, epsilon zero
is 8.8 10 to the minus 12,

00:48:50.750 --> 00:48:59.110
and here should be
coulomb epsilon here

00:48:59.110 --> 00:49:00.355
is farad per meter.

00:49:03.720 --> 00:49:05.860
OK.

00:49:05.860 --> 00:49:10.980
So I have this one
is a farad per meter.

00:49:10.980 --> 00:49:12.210
OK.

00:49:12.210 --> 00:49:14.850
So I have the--

00:49:14.850 --> 00:49:21.100
this is D here, the
displacement field.

00:49:21.100 --> 00:49:26.670
I said that this is
the one external field

00:49:26.670 --> 00:49:29.395
create a dipole, right?

00:49:29.395 --> 00:49:31.470
This is real solid.

00:49:31.470 --> 00:49:34.710
It's not that simple
because you have atom here,

00:49:34.710 --> 00:49:36.570
you have another atom here.

00:49:36.570 --> 00:49:39.180
You have adjacent atoms.

00:49:39.180 --> 00:49:41.950
And not only are
they outside field,

00:49:41.950 --> 00:49:43.920
but also the next
labor, the dipole

00:49:43.920 --> 00:49:47.740
itself will affect
the atom itself.

00:49:47.740 --> 00:49:52.660
So it's actually a summation
of all this effect.

00:49:52.660 --> 00:49:57.730
And this one, this is
a non-movable charge.

00:49:57.730 --> 00:50:02.070
This is the charge
attached to the atom.

00:50:02.070 --> 00:50:03.990
That's dielectric.

00:50:03.990 --> 00:50:07.380
So we sometimes
write the epsilon.

00:50:07.380 --> 00:50:13.440
Epsilon r times E. Well,
this combined together

00:50:13.440 --> 00:50:15.630
gives me another epsilon.

00:50:15.630 --> 00:50:20.480
That's a dielectric
function of the material.

00:50:20.480 --> 00:50:21.440
It's not a constant.

00:50:21.440 --> 00:50:23.150
Sometimes we call it
dielectric constant.

00:50:23.150 --> 00:50:25.360
It's not a constant.

00:50:25.360 --> 00:50:27.010
It's a function of wave lengths.

00:50:27.010 --> 00:50:30.600
It's a function of frequency.

00:50:30.600 --> 00:50:32.230
OK.

00:50:32.230 --> 00:50:35.660
So that's the displacement.

00:50:35.660 --> 00:50:37.810
And similarly,
[INAUDIBLE] induction,

00:50:37.810 --> 00:50:43.330
B, you can write it as a
epsilon vacuum, a mu vacuum,

00:50:43.330 --> 00:50:49.090
mu r times H. This is
just like we're writing

00:50:49.090 --> 00:50:51.220
to the displacement field.

00:50:51.220 --> 00:50:55.150
It's the electric field times
the dielectric constant.

00:50:55.150 --> 00:50:58.690
And here is the
vacuum permittivity,

00:50:58.690 --> 00:51:00.520
the relative to vacuum.

00:51:00.520 --> 00:51:03.550
Most materials are at
high visible wavelengths

00:51:03.550 --> 00:51:05.050
or high frequency.

00:51:05.050 --> 00:51:06.790
This one is about one.

00:51:06.790 --> 00:51:08.620
It doesn't have
magnetic response.

00:51:08.620 --> 00:51:11.070
Most materials.

00:51:11.070 --> 00:51:13.500
At a low frequency,
you have magnet.

00:51:13.500 --> 00:51:15.300
But say high frequency,
most material

00:51:15.300 --> 00:51:19.440
don't have the
magnetic response.

00:51:19.440 --> 00:51:22.020
And in fact, that was
the basis of an invention

00:51:22.020 --> 00:51:27.390
made by Professor [INAUDIBLE].

00:51:27.390 --> 00:51:32.990
He was trying to think about
how do you get a powerless--

00:51:32.990 --> 00:51:36.530
wireless, cordless
power transfer.

00:51:36.530 --> 00:51:41.150
And the problem is if you
want to beam a lot of power

00:51:41.150 --> 00:51:43.520
through this space
we'll all be cooked.

00:51:43.520 --> 00:51:46.520
We have dielectric
response, right?

00:51:46.520 --> 00:51:50.090
Microwave, you heat it up.

00:51:50.090 --> 00:51:53.060
But say because materials
at a high frequency

00:51:53.060 --> 00:51:56.120
don't have magnetic
response, so you

00:51:56.120 --> 00:52:01.530
thought about using a magnetic
field to deliver the power.

00:52:01.530 --> 00:52:05.210
So we have the start up.

00:52:05.210 --> 00:52:07.440
Try and commercialize that.

00:52:07.440 --> 00:52:08.760
OK.

00:52:08.760 --> 00:52:13.290
So that's the basic equations.

00:52:13.290 --> 00:52:17.790
And a few more comments.

00:52:17.790 --> 00:52:20.970
The relation between current--

00:52:20.970 --> 00:52:23.310
that's a real current,
a free electron.

00:52:23.310 --> 00:52:25.440
The current flow.

00:52:25.440 --> 00:52:27.820
And current, of course, is
related to electric field

00:52:27.820 --> 00:52:33.750
through if you have a conductor
or semiconductor, that's

00:52:33.750 --> 00:52:34.500
the Ohm's law.

00:52:41.630 --> 00:52:45.710
So j equals electric
conductivity.

00:52:45.710 --> 00:52:48.020
That's Ohm's law.

00:52:48.020 --> 00:52:50.930
Electric conductivity is sigma.

00:52:50.930 --> 00:53:00.040
And here, the unit is
inverse ohm, centimeter.

00:53:00.040 --> 00:53:02.373
Right?

00:53:02.373 --> 00:53:03.040
Ohm, centimeter.

00:53:03.040 --> 00:53:03.540
Yeah.

00:53:03.540 --> 00:53:05.810
Inverse.

00:53:05.810 --> 00:53:07.180
No.

00:53:07.180 --> 00:53:08.690
It should be inverse.

00:53:14.220 --> 00:53:21.140
So inverse ohm is also same
m per meter, different units.

00:53:21.140 --> 00:53:24.220
If you don't use it often,
it's very confusing.

00:53:24.220 --> 00:53:24.720
OK.

00:53:24.720 --> 00:53:27.160
So we have all these quantities.

00:53:27.160 --> 00:53:30.270
And further, what
is the epsilon,

00:53:30.270 --> 00:53:33.570
let's say, the charge density.

00:53:33.570 --> 00:53:34.410
OK.

00:53:34.410 --> 00:53:38.730
And this charge density
is the lab charge

00:53:38.730 --> 00:53:41.980
per unit volume in the material.

00:53:41.980 --> 00:53:47.070
OK, so if you have
a semiconductor,

00:53:47.070 --> 00:53:53.550
you know, semiconductor you
can have a positive donor, say,

00:53:53.550 --> 00:53:55.980
if you put a phosphor there.

00:53:55.980 --> 00:53:58.860
OK, so let's say put
that phosphor atom

00:53:58.860 --> 00:54:01.590
in silicon and phosphor atom.

00:54:01.590 --> 00:54:03.720
Lose the electron.

00:54:03.720 --> 00:54:09.210
So the atom itself is immobile,
electron becomes immobile.

00:54:09.210 --> 00:54:12.940
So what do you need is
this is a positive charge.

00:54:12.940 --> 00:54:15.090
You also have
electronegative charge.

00:54:15.090 --> 00:54:19.320
You add them all together,
that's per unit volume.

00:54:19.320 --> 00:54:21.880
How much charge you have?

00:54:21.880 --> 00:54:27.490
So these are the set
of equations describing

00:54:27.490 --> 00:54:31.280
the electromagnetic waves.

00:54:31.280 --> 00:54:37.510
And now we can see why.

00:54:37.510 --> 00:54:42.610
Let's do a few math operation
just to get familiar with it.

00:54:42.610 --> 00:54:44.210
You have seen them.

00:54:44.210 --> 00:54:51.970
So if I look at this, I
will first eliminate a--

00:54:51.970 --> 00:54:58.420
because the B right here,
I can write as a mu h.

00:54:58.420 --> 00:55:00.940
Mu zero times mu r is mu.

00:55:00.940 --> 00:55:03.280
And permittivity.

00:55:03.280 --> 00:55:05.660
And so B equals mu h.

00:55:05.660 --> 00:55:07.210
So I used the first one.

00:55:07.210 --> 00:55:20.320
I get the first equation, delta
across E equals mass D mu h Dt.

00:55:20.320 --> 00:55:22.480
That's the first equation.

00:55:22.480 --> 00:55:28.030
And the second equation,
I have delta across H,

00:55:28.030 --> 00:55:36.550
E across D, Dt,
and epsilon times

00:55:36.550 --> 00:55:41.710
E. This is a dielectric
function, which

00:55:41.710 --> 00:55:46.840
is epsilon zero times epsilon
r, the displacement field

00:55:46.840 --> 00:55:53.480
plus sigma times E.

00:55:53.480 --> 00:55:56.630
Those are the-- if I
use considered relations

00:55:56.630 --> 00:56:02.945
and eliminate B and D,
I got the equation here.

00:56:05.490 --> 00:56:07.950
And let me first
to drop this term.

00:56:10.500 --> 00:56:13.350
Let's consider a dielectric.

00:56:13.350 --> 00:56:18.120
There's no free charge
in the material,

00:56:18.120 --> 00:56:21.480
so electrical
conductivity is zero.

00:56:21.480 --> 00:56:26.820
With that I can plug
this H into here,

00:56:26.820 --> 00:56:31.680
and I take a time
derivative on both sides,

00:56:31.680 --> 00:56:37.950
and then I gather D, H. So
this is assuming mu and epsilon

00:56:37.950 --> 00:56:39.270
are independent of time.

00:56:42.170 --> 00:56:45.020
And if it depends on time,
you have to be careful.

00:56:45.020 --> 00:56:46.410
[PHONE RINGING]

00:56:46.410 --> 00:56:47.368
That's not mine, right?

00:56:47.368 --> 00:56:48.170
AUDIENCE: Sorry.

00:56:48.170 --> 00:56:51.140
GANG CHEN: Oh, OK.

00:56:51.140 --> 00:56:58.880
So if I eliminate--

00:56:58.880 --> 00:57:04.730
if I take this epsilon mu out,
I'll be independent of time.

00:57:04.730 --> 00:57:07.850
And sometimes you
have to be careful,

00:57:07.850 --> 00:57:11.510
because when you do those kind
of mathematical operations,

00:57:11.510 --> 00:57:18.300
you make assumptions, you may
lose the big opportunities, OK?

00:57:18.300 --> 00:57:24.300
And this is the
electromagnetic field.

00:57:24.300 --> 00:57:26.260
There are a lot of
new concepts that

00:57:26.260 --> 00:57:31.150
is all based on going back
to the original equation

00:57:31.150 --> 00:57:34.650
and relook at
them, and say are--

00:57:37.800 --> 00:57:40.530
where are the
approximations made?

00:57:40.530 --> 00:57:45.840
You were reading Yablonovitch
chapter, essay, paper

00:57:45.840 --> 00:57:48.810
on photonic crystal, right?

00:57:48.810 --> 00:57:56.730
And his photonic
crystal is really--

00:57:56.730 --> 00:58:00.690
that's the concept in that case,
the epsilon, which we typically

00:58:00.690 --> 00:58:05.900
take as uniform,
but he was really

00:58:05.900 --> 00:58:09.980
taking this uniform epsilon
as a periodic function.

00:58:09.980 --> 00:58:14.500
So he put the epsilon
as a periodic function,

00:58:14.500 --> 00:58:19.150
and that's like a periodic
potential for atoms.

00:58:19.150 --> 00:58:23.110
If you think about that when we
saw the band gap of electrons

00:58:23.110 --> 00:58:27.190
for Schrodinger equation,
that come from the fact

00:58:27.190 --> 00:58:32.080
that the potential for
electrons is periodic.

00:58:32.080 --> 00:58:39.290
Maxwell's equation itself,
there is no potential here.

00:58:39.290 --> 00:58:42.410
He put this one
epsilon as a constant,

00:58:42.410 --> 00:58:44.940
and then he was really
using the analogy.

00:58:44.940 --> 00:58:49.640
And in fact, I spent--

00:58:49.640 --> 00:58:51.440
on day, I was in Berlin.

00:58:51.440 --> 00:58:54.960
We both of us were
wandering in the city.

00:58:54.960 --> 00:58:56.550
So I was talking to him.

00:58:56.550 --> 00:58:59.060
He said that when he
conceived the concept

00:58:59.060 --> 00:59:04.130
of photonic crystal,
he wrote the paper.

00:59:04.130 --> 00:59:05.270
So photonic crystal.

00:59:05.270 --> 00:59:10.010
What is-- a photonic crystal is
basically periodic arrangement

00:59:10.010 --> 00:59:11.930
of whatever--

00:59:11.930 --> 00:59:13.100
glass beads.

00:59:13.100 --> 00:59:15.410
You can think about that, right?

00:59:15.410 --> 00:59:23.540
And if you look at the
evolution, in ball crystal,

00:59:23.540 --> 00:59:25.580
we have band gap.

00:59:25.580 --> 00:59:32.090
And in the '70s,
there is this concept

00:59:32.090 --> 00:59:36.260
of a superlattice,
quantum wells.

00:59:36.260 --> 00:59:40.020
You read, again,
[INAUDIBLE] paper.

00:59:40.020 --> 00:59:45.080
And that's put in multi
layers of thin films.

00:59:45.080 --> 00:59:47.300
That makes the one dimension.

00:59:47.300 --> 00:59:48.450
You got the artificial.

00:59:48.450 --> 00:59:52.790
This is where we draw the
potential, purely potential.

00:59:52.790 --> 00:59:55.280
That's the [INAUDIBLE] and
panning model we talked before,

00:59:55.280 --> 00:59:56.960
but it's artificial material.

00:59:56.960 --> 01:00:04.350
So you go from three dimensional
crystal purely potential to 1D,

01:00:04.350 --> 01:00:07.200
and that's a big jump
in concept because

01:00:07.200 --> 01:00:10.680
of the artificial
quantum structures.

01:00:10.680 --> 01:00:17.310
And on the other hand, in
optics, you have the latter.

01:00:17.310 --> 01:00:20.570
Over a hundred years, people
know how to do coding.

01:00:20.570 --> 01:00:22.520
People have been
doing, refining optics

01:00:22.520 --> 01:00:25.670
to code multilayer films.

01:00:25.670 --> 01:00:27.410
Some of this is purely--

01:00:27.410 --> 01:00:33.120
I will say anti-reflection or
purely reflecting the purpose.

01:00:33.120 --> 01:00:38.900
And so the reason, so you have
those multilayer, thin film

01:00:38.900 --> 01:00:42.830
coatings, which is typically
of the order of quarter

01:00:42.830 --> 01:00:44.560
wavelengths.

01:00:44.560 --> 01:00:48.990
And you can code this so that
it's complete reflection.

01:00:48.990 --> 01:00:50.370
What is a complete reflection?

01:00:50.370 --> 01:00:52.560
It is the wave function
of electromagnetic wave

01:00:52.560 --> 01:00:53.850
zero inside.

01:00:53.850 --> 01:00:55.640
That's forbidden.

01:00:55.640 --> 01:00:57.860
There's a band gap in 1D.

01:01:00.420 --> 01:01:04.170
So what I will always propose
as a photonic crystal,

01:01:04.170 --> 01:01:07.860
is how to make
this back into 3D.

01:01:07.860 --> 01:01:12.170
What laser has is
electron photons in 3D,

01:01:12.170 --> 01:01:18.620
and say, researchers, we have
created this 1D structure.

01:01:18.620 --> 01:01:21.830
So that's what you see is
the opposite direction going.

01:01:21.830 --> 01:01:26.690
And here is trying to make
photonic analogy of some field

01:01:26.690 --> 01:01:28.280
to 3D.

01:01:28.280 --> 01:01:28.780
OK.

01:01:28.780 --> 01:01:30.550
So he said that when
he wrote the paper,

01:01:30.550 --> 01:01:35.910
you go to read his paper
and there's no math inside.

01:01:35.910 --> 01:01:38.220
It was just a concept.

01:01:38.220 --> 01:01:42.090
And he submitted a paper.

01:01:42.090 --> 01:01:47.700
And he knows who he
wants to be reviewer.

01:01:47.700 --> 01:01:49.440
And his friend
said, do you really

01:01:49.440 --> 01:01:50.565
want to publish this paper?

01:01:53.820 --> 01:01:56.670
This is a really--

01:01:56.670 --> 01:01:59.145
it doesn't look like a paper.

01:01:59.145 --> 01:02:00.270
He said, it doesn't matter.

01:02:00.270 --> 01:02:01.780
Just publish it.

01:02:01.780 --> 01:02:05.640
So that's what you read.

01:02:05.640 --> 01:02:10.110
It's the beginning of a new
field, photonic crystal.

01:02:10.110 --> 01:02:11.880
OK.

01:02:11.880 --> 01:02:14.850
So epsilon is a function of r.

01:02:14.850 --> 01:02:17.010
Periodic, right?

01:02:17.010 --> 01:02:19.540
And epsilon could also
be a function of time.

01:02:19.540 --> 01:02:22.680
In fact, I was doing some--

01:02:22.680 --> 01:02:26.220
when I did my
graduate school study,

01:02:26.220 --> 01:02:30.510
I never came up with big ideas,
but once I was writing down

01:02:30.510 --> 01:02:36.600
the loads, I said, OK,
because I was doing some stuff

01:02:36.600 --> 01:02:40.020
during the optical, say
the [INAUDIBLE] laser

01:02:40.020 --> 01:02:41.700
material interaction.

01:02:41.700 --> 01:02:43.620
During that process,
the epsilon wall

01:02:43.620 --> 01:02:45.480
changed as a function
of temperature,

01:02:45.480 --> 01:02:47.460
and temperature changed
as a function of time,

01:02:47.460 --> 01:02:49.050
so I have to keep that there.

01:02:49.050 --> 01:02:50.850
I wrote all those equations.

01:02:50.850 --> 01:02:53.580
And a few years later,
my friend asked me,

01:02:53.580 --> 01:02:55.860
I said, actually,
it's in my notes.

01:02:55.860 --> 01:02:58.330
But it never got anywhere.

01:02:58.330 --> 01:03:01.290
So one story.

01:03:01.290 --> 01:03:04.110
But anyway, let's continue here.

01:03:04.110 --> 01:03:05.220
I have two equations.

01:03:05.220 --> 01:03:06.750
I drop this.

01:03:06.750 --> 01:03:07.770
I'm going to name that--

01:03:07.770 --> 01:03:11.160
I say mu epsilon constant.

01:03:11.160 --> 01:03:13.920
And I'm going to
then put it out.

01:03:13.920 --> 01:03:17.310
And I can eliminate H.
And what I have here

01:03:17.310 --> 01:03:20.410
then is the equation.

01:03:20.410 --> 01:03:29.220
So if I eliminate H, I have
a delta across E over a mu.

01:03:29.220 --> 01:03:35.320
And here, I have epsilon.

01:03:38.070 --> 01:03:40.470
I start to get a wave equation.

01:03:44.130 --> 01:03:49.290
And you can use the
vector operation

01:03:49.290 --> 01:03:52.965
to rewrite this into--

01:04:02.450 --> 01:04:07.130
if you use a vector
relation, you will get--

01:04:07.130 --> 01:04:09.650
actually, there is a
negative sign in the front.

01:04:09.650 --> 01:04:19.310
And delta epsilon square,
mu epsilon, DE, Dt square.

01:04:19.310 --> 01:04:28.410
And if I continue to carry that,
it will be mu sigma DE, Dt.

01:04:28.410 --> 01:04:28.910
OK.

01:04:28.910 --> 01:04:30.440
This is the one.

01:04:30.440 --> 01:04:36.710
I carry the metal term,
the conductivity term.

01:04:36.710 --> 01:04:39.260
If I don't, I have a
pure wave equation.

01:04:39.260 --> 01:04:42.800
If I drop this, you can say
this is a wave equation.

01:04:42.800 --> 01:04:46.370
Second order in space,
second order in time,

01:04:46.370 --> 01:04:50.180
unlike the Schrodinger
equation, which

01:04:50.180 --> 01:04:52.790
is the first order in time,
but has an imaginary number

01:04:52.790 --> 01:04:54.420
in the front.

01:04:54.420 --> 01:04:56.280
Now I have a real wave equation.

01:04:56.280 --> 01:04:58.590
It's the second order
in both space and time.

01:05:01.730 --> 01:05:06.300
So this is the Maxwell equation.

01:05:06.300 --> 01:05:13.130
And if you look at the typical
wave solution, plane wave,

01:05:13.130 --> 01:05:19.920
epsilon is a function of r
and t, and this is a vector,

01:05:19.920 --> 01:05:24.630
so that's the polarization
direction, the electrical field

01:05:24.630 --> 01:05:28.460
direction, and this is
the propagation direction,

01:05:28.460 --> 01:05:32.050
omega t minus k dot r.

01:05:34.790 --> 01:05:39.530
So this is a plane
wave expression.

01:05:39.530 --> 01:05:40.820
We talked before.

01:05:40.820 --> 01:05:43.430
And the assumption back
into here, you will say,

01:05:43.430 --> 01:05:44.900
is satisfying the wave equation.

01:05:48.450 --> 01:05:53.250
And in fact, if you do it,
if you substitute it back,

01:05:53.250 --> 01:05:56.550
say the left hand side is
the second order derivative

01:05:56.550 --> 01:05:59.370
in space, so I'll get k squared.

01:05:59.370 --> 01:06:06.390
So I will get k dot k.

01:06:06.390 --> 01:06:10.710
And the right hand side, I
will get a mu omega squared.

01:06:10.710 --> 01:06:12.430
This is time.

01:06:12.430 --> 01:06:19.980
And epsilon plus
i sigma and omega.

01:06:19.980 --> 01:06:23.220
This is this term combined
with the first term.

01:06:23.220 --> 01:06:26.220
And the rest, i omega
t, this term cancel,

01:06:26.220 --> 01:06:29.820
the phase factor all cancel.

01:06:29.820 --> 01:06:30.840
OK.

01:06:30.840 --> 01:06:36.870
And this way, I can
write the expression as,

01:06:36.870 --> 01:06:43.920
because omega squared, so I have
mu epsilon tilde omega squared.

01:06:43.920 --> 01:06:48.870
The wave vector is
proportional to omega.

01:06:48.870 --> 01:06:54.630
For a wave in free space,
this is epsilon zero, mu zero.

01:06:54.630 --> 01:06:55.305
Free space.

01:06:57.920 --> 01:07:02.840
And this is what the triumph
of electromagnetic wave,

01:07:02.840 --> 01:07:08.815
because Maxwell's equation
predicted the speed of light.

01:07:11.720 --> 01:07:12.620
OK.

01:07:12.620 --> 01:07:18.470
Because when you do this,
you get the magnitude,

01:07:18.470 --> 01:07:24.380
k squared equals
omega divided by--

01:07:24.380 --> 01:07:31.910
here, I do the square
root of epsilon tilde, mu.

01:07:31.910 --> 01:07:37.445
And this one, we
can write it into--

01:07:49.000 --> 01:07:54.010
so I can write it k,
the magnitude of--

01:07:54.010 --> 01:07:56.140
this is not square.

01:07:56.140 --> 01:07:57.470
The magnitude.

01:07:57.470 --> 01:08:09.210
So the magnitude of k
equals omega times C. Ck.

01:08:09.210 --> 01:08:10.260
Omega equals Ck.

01:08:10.260 --> 01:08:12.560
That's the dispersion.

01:08:12.560 --> 01:08:19.069
And C is square root of
epsilon tilde and mu.

01:08:19.069 --> 01:08:24.500
And typically, I would
define refractive index

01:08:24.500 --> 01:08:28.941
as the speed of light in vacuum
divided by speed of light

01:08:28.941 --> 01:08:29.524
in the medium.

01:08:32.330 --> 01:08:35.810
And the speed of light in
vacuum, this is epsilon 0,

01:08:35.810 --> 01:08:44.180
mu zero, and it's approximated
because most high frequency

01:08:44.180 --> 01:08:45.859
magnetic response is 1.

01:08:45.859 --> 01:08:50.450
So this is epsilon
tilde over epsilon 0.

01:08:50.450 --> 01:08:55.370
And this one is epsilon r.

01:08:55.370 --> 01:09:01.750
So even for metals,
very often we tabulate.

01:09:01.750 --> 01:09:04.420
We don't tabulate
these two separately.

01:09:04.420 --> 01:09:08.560
We just tabulate them
together into epsilon r,

01:09:08.560 --> 01:09:12.460
the relative
dielectric constant.

01:09:12.460 --> 01:09:22.149
OK so there are a few
interesting stories here again.

01:09:22.149 --> 01:09:23.490
OK.

01:09:23.490 --> 01:09:29.819
You take a positive square
root going from here to here.

01:09:29.819 --> 01:09:35.700
You take a square root, and then
say that's a natural solution.

01:09:35.700 --> 01:09:38.894
And if you go to look at
your Maxwell equation,

01:09:38.894 --> 01:09:42.090
it turns out that this wave,
it's a right-hand wave.

01:09:42.090 --> 01:09:45.960
So say this is
epsilon E direction,

01:09:45.960 --> 01:09:48.600
electric field direction.

01:09:48.600 --> 01:09:50.160
It's a transverse wave.

01:09:50.160 --> 01:09:51.960
This is what the
equation tells you.

01:09:51.960 --> 01:09:53.460
Go, you check.

01:09:53.460 --> 01:09:56.130
It's a transverse
wave, so electric field

01:09:56.130 --> 01:09:59.670
will be perpendicular
to a magnetic field,

01:09:59.670 --> 01:10:03.870
will be perpendicular to k,
the wave vector direction,

01:10:03.870 --> 01:10:06.510
k, the wave propagation
there, right?

01:10:06.510 --> 01:10:10.260
That's why it's a
transverse wave.

01:10:10.260 --> 01:10:15.510
So now the only transverse
wave is also a right-hand wave.

01:10:15.510 --> 01:10:17.790
What the right
hand mean is if you

01:10:17.790 --> 01:10:21.570
recall when you learned
those, say, as E across h

01:10:21.570 --> 01:10:25.990
goes to the wave
propagation direction.

01:10:25.990 --> 01:10:29.260
So there's a right-hand
side, your E direction.

01:10:29.260 --> 01:10:31.750
You grab to the h
direction then some point

01:10:31.750 --> 01:10:34.570
to do the k direction.

01:10:34.570 --> 01:10:36.370
OK.

01:10:36.370 --> 01:10:38.500
So it's a right-hand wave.

01:10:38.500 --> 01:10:40.420
It's a transverse wave.

01:10:40.420 --> 01:10:47.330
Except I say we ignore
the possibility of when

01:10:47.330 --> 01:10:53.740
you take this k square
root, it could be a negative

01:10:53.740 --> 01:10:55.105
also, root solution.

01:10:58.370 --> 01:11:03.250
Negative solution
typically are ruled out,

01:11:03.250 --> 01:11:10.300
but if when epsilon and mu could
be negative, when both of them

01:11:10.300 --> 01:11:12.850
could be negative, it
turns out that you go back

01:11:12.850 --> 01:11:18.190
to check the equation again, you
have to take a negative root.

01:11:18.190 --> 01:11:23.110
So this effect was
predicted in 1950s

01:11:23.110 --> 01:11:27.060
by Russian scientist
[INAUDIBLE]..

01:11:27.060 --> 01:11:32.170
And his paper was
soon forgotten.

01:11:32.170 --> 01:11:33.220
OK.

01:11:33.220 --> 01:11:39.080
By the '90s, people start
to pay attention to it.

01:11:39.080 --> 01:11:42.620
First, they are
natural materials

01:11:42.620 --> 01:11:44.090
with the epsilon negative.

01:11:44.090 --> 01:11:46.295
It just doesn't have
natural materials with mu

01:11:46.295 --> 01:11:47.840
equals negative.

01:11:47.840 --> 01:11:51.650
Why the natural material
could have epsilon negative?

01:11:51.650 --> 01:11:54.830
Epsilon, remember,
is the response

01:11:54.830 --> 01:11:57.680
of the material-- oh,
I think I erased it.

01:11:57.680 --> 01:12:01.220
When you have electric field,
the material will polarize.

01:12:01.220 --> 01:12:04.445
If it's an electron,
for example, and then

01:12:04.445 --> 01:12:07.730
when you have an external
wave comes in oscillating,

01:12:07.730 --> 01:12:10.550
the electron creates a
resistance, say, direction

01:12:10.550 --> 01:12:12.080
and field.

01:12:12.080 --> 01:12:14.750
And if that field is
larger than the incident,

01:12:14.750 --> 01:12:19.420
you get the negative
direction displacement.

01:12:19.420 --> 01:12:21.190
So the epsilon becomes negative.

01:12:21.190 --> 01:12:24.880
But there's no material
with the mu negative.

01:12:24.880 --> 01:12:29.500
Then, say, in
'90s, people design

01:12:29.500 --> 01:12:33.610
this artificial resonator
structure that created,

01:12:33.610 --> 01:12:36.400
generated a, say,
artificial magnetic.

01:12:36.400 --> 01:12:41.670
So you basically create
a loop with a gap.

01:12:41.670 --> 01:12:46.470
And when the electric current
oscillate in this loop,

01:12:46.470 --> 01:12:48.390
they generate magnetic field.

01:12:48.390 --> 01:12:50.520
And when you make
them very small,

01:12:50.520 --> 01:12:54.240
the magnetic field could
be very, very fast.

01:12:54.240 --> 01:12:56.430
Make it smaller.

01:12:56.430 --> 01:12:58.870
And if you bring
both epsilon and mu

01:12:58.870 --> 01:13:01.530
negative within the
same frequency range,

01:13:01.530 --> 01:13:04.720
you have to go to take
that negative root.

01:13:04.720 --> 01:13:07.030
So become a
left-handed material.

01:13:07.030 --> 01:13:11.300
So E across h, k
goes the other way.

